  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/0d329269-7dd0-4252-90be-61da36aa19df.png\" style=\"width:2.14028in;height:1.32708in\" /><br />One of the end of latus rectum is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Tangent at <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />Area of rhombus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8901;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8901;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the required area <math><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;sq. units</p>",
